---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PricingTable from '../components/PricingTable.astro';
import { wi, wa } from '../data/site.js';
import pricing from '../data/pricing.json';
---
<Base title="Prewarmed Inbox & Domain Pricing — Google, Microsoft 365, Azure"
      description="Pricing for prewarmed Google Workspace, Microsoft 365 and Azure tenant inboxes, plus fresh inboxes and standalone prewarmed domains.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:900px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
      <h1>What it costs</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every price below renders from a single data file so nothing drifts out of step with warminboxes.com. Longer billing periods cost less per inbox.</p>
      {!pricing._verified && (
        <p class="unver mono">These figures are marked unverified in the source data and the live build is blocked until someone confirms them against warminboxes.com.</p>
      )}
      <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Prewarmed inboxes</h2>
      <PricingTable productKey="google-prewarmed" />
      <PricingTable productKey="microsoft-prewarmed" />
      <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Azure tenants</h2>
      <p class="muted">A hundred mailboxes behind one admin. Far cheaper per inbox, and one shared reputation — see the <a href="/prewarmed-azure-inboxes/">Azure page</a> for the risk model before buying.</p>
      <PricingTable productKey="azure-tenant" />
      <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Fresh inboxes</h2>
      <p class="muted">No aging, no warming, no domain. You do the 51 days. Priced accordingly. See <a href="/fresh-google-inboxes/">fresh Google inboxes</a> and <a href="/fresh-microsoft-365-inboxes/">fresh Microsoft 365 inboxes</a> for what you take on.</p>
      <PricingTable productKey="google-fresh" />
      <PricingTable productKey="microsoft-fresh" />
      <p class="muted"><strong>Fresh Azure tenants</strong> — 100 unwarmed mailboxes under one admin — are priced per tenant and not listed here yet. See <a href="/fresh-azure-inboxes/">fresh Azure tenants</a>, and work out what warming a hundred mailboxes costs you before ordering: it is usually the number that decides it.</p>
      <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Notes</h2>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li>Prewarmed packs include a prewarmed .com or .co domain at no cost.</li>
        <li>Non-.com prewarmed domains from ${pricing.policy.nonComFrom} via support.</li>
        <li><strong>Domains.</strong> A prewarmed .com is included free with every inbox pack. A <a href="/fresh-domains/">fresh .com</a> is ${pricing.products['domain-fresh'].price} per domain, one-time. Aged .com domains are quoted individually — <a href={wa('Hi — I am looking for aged .com domains. Here is what I need:')}>message us</a> with what you need.</li>
        <li>{pricing.policy.delivery}.</li>
        <li><strong>Refunds:</strong> see <a href="/refund-policy/">the refund policy</a>. Read it before ordering.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top:32px"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={wi('/', { page: 'pricing', placement: 'body' })}>Order at Warm Inboxes</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  h1 { margin: 12px 0 18px; }
  .unver { font-size: 13px; color: var(--warning); background: var(--warning-soft); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--warning) 35%, transparent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-top: 22px; }
  .notes { padding-left: 20px; color: var(--text-2); }
  .notes li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
</style>
